Title: ticket-sweep.sh merged-probe exits 2 where git or the forge can settle
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-11-09T19:17Z haduong created

--- body ---
## Context

Found by the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09 (19:05-19:15 UTC, run
from the ~/CNRS session). `scripts/ticket-sweep.sh merged-probe` exits 2
(could-not-determine) on branches git or the forge can settle, so molt never
cleans them.

## Evidence

- (a) Default branch `master`: chemin-de-voix, every branch exits 2 with
  "git could not compare <branch> with main", including
  `codex/1463-check-fast`, a plain ancestor of origin/master.
- (b) Squash-landed branches whose ticket's `Closed:` line names no PR:
  padme `t0106-btrbk-cold`, search-works-for-zotero `t1141` and
  `ticket/0811`, chemin-de-voix `t1141`. `git cherry` and `git range-diff`
  show them landed.
- (c) Branches that map to no ticket by name: AEDIST's 78
  `tournament/<id>-*` branches; livre-milliards-climat has no `tickets/` at
  all, while the forge shows its PR #3 closed unmerged.

## Diagnosis

Established: exit 2 in all three classes, with the observations above. Not
established: whether (a) is a hard-coded `main` or a missing `origin/HEAD`
lookup; whether (c) should be settled by the probe or left to molt.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The probe detects the default branch (origin/HEAD, else main/master) instead of assuming `main`
- [ ] Patch-id evidence (`git cherry` all `-`, or equivalent) is accepted as a second landed signal
- [ ] A forge closed-unmerged state yields exit 1 (not merged), not 2
- [ ] Tests cover (a), (b) and (c)
